WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:05.440
Superpowered farts and an island of mutated&nbsp;
beasts don't make for an easy trip down&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:10.910
memory lane. Not even a vanishing spell can&nbsp;
wipe these box office flops from history.

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:16.560
The late British actor John Hurt played a number&nbsp;
of iconic parts in his long career, with key roles&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:22.880
in classic fantasy and sci-fi franchises like&nbsp;
"Doctor Who," "Alien," "Hellboy," and of course&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:27.200
the "Harry Potter" films, where he played&nbsp;
Garrick Ollivander. But there's at least one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:32.880
film he starred in back in the '90s that failed&nbsp;
to take hold and become the next big sci-fi film,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:37.760
instead becoming a flop. That&nbsp;
was the 1993 movie "Monolith."

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:42.240
The film focuses on a pair of police officers&nbsp;
who are investigating the passing of a young boy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:47.040
when they stumble across a possible alien&nbsp;
invader with the ability to shapeshift.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:50.720
Hurt portrays the government agent who&nbsp;
wants them to leave the case alone.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.720 --> 00:00:56.000
Though it does have some genuinely intriguing&nbsp;
ideas, it all comes across so generic and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:01.120
ham-fisted that it becomes a whole lot of&nbsp;
nothing. Bad direction, bland characters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:07.120
a confusing script … We've seen it all before in&nbsp;
bad B-movies that were better than this. Hurt is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:12.320
certainly capable of playing a chilling, even&nbsp;
terrifying villain, but he's woefully miscast&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.320 --> 00:01:16.960
in "Monolith" and would probably have&nbsp;
wanted us to forget he was ever in it.

00:01:16.960 --> 00:01:20.240
Helena Bonham Carter would join&nbsp;
the "Harry Potter" series in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:25.120
"The Order Of The Phoenix" and return for its&nbsp;
three sequels as the villainous Death Eater&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:30.640
Bellatrix Lestrange. It was a part that seems&nbsp;
like it was tailor made for the frenetic actress.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:35.680
One-time partner of Tim Burton, she has also&nbsp;
starred in more than a half-dozen of his films,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.680 --> 00:01:39.760
including "Planet of the Apes," "Alice&nbsp;
in Wonderland," and "Dark Shadows."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.760 --> 00:01:44.880
Across her career she's ventured into just about&nbsp;
every genre and dozens of acclaimed movies. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:51.040
if she could wipe one of them from existence, it&nbsp;
has to be the strange dental comedy "Novocaine."

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:56.000
The film is about a dentist who gets framed for&nbsp;
murder after an encounter with alluring patient,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.000 --> 00:02:01.520
played by Carter, who seduces him and turns&nbsp;
his life upside down. A tonal mish-mash,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:06.320
the movie dances between black comedy and&nbsp;
outright parody, making one increasingly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.320 --> 00:02:11.600
numb to its ambitious premise. Whether it's&nbsp;
supposed to be a genuinely suspenseful thriller or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:17.120
a comic farce you're never quite sure, but when&nbsp;
it's all over you just want to rinse and spit.

00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:19.200
"You see, that's the nature of attraction.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:23.100
You find yourself doing things&nbsp;
and you have no idea why."

00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:28.320
Before "Harry Potter," Alan Rickman already&nbsp;
had several well-known roles under his belt,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:31.920
including the Sheriff of Nottingham&nbsp;
in "Robin Hood: Prince of Thieves"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:36.400
and the villainous Hans Gruber in the&nbsp;
action classic "Die Hard." But he'd reach&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:41.600
a new stratosphere in the "Harry Potter" series&nbsp;
portraying the dark, enigmatic Professor Snape,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.600 --> 00:02:46.560
a wizard who seemed to blur the line between&nbsp;
good and evil. Already a Hollywood fixture,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:50.320
the role further cemented Rickman&nbsp;
as one of Hollywood's finest stars.

00:02:50.320 --> 00:02:55.040
But Rickman wasn't without his duds, and&nbsp;
few can measure up to the disappointment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.040 --> 00:03:01.200
of "Mesmer," a bizarre biopic about Franz Anton&nbsp;
Mesmer. Mesmer was a doctor who peddled his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:06.560
theories in hypnosis and mystical energies in&nbsp;
the 18th century. The result is a film that's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.560 --> 00:03:12.080
about what you'd expect from a period drama based&nbsp;
on a forgotten figure in pseudoscience history,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.080 --> 00:03:16.080
even if Rickman is his usual&nbsp;
charismatic self in the title role.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.080 --> 00:03:20.240
Still, the actor alone often can't&nbsp;
save a film, though he tried.

00:03:20.240 --> 00:03:22.203
"That's very kind of you."

00:03:22.203 --> 00:03:27.200
Before Ralph Fiennes played a heroic,&nbsp;
old-fashioned superspy in "The King's Man,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:33.120
the actor who starred in "Harry Potter" as Lord&nbsp;
Voldemort led a flop called "The Avengers." It's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:37.600
a movie that Fiennes and pretty much everyone&nbsp;
else involved would be thrilled to forget,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.600 --> 00:03:43.360
as it is one of the most notorious film failures&nbsp;
of the '90s. Not only was it a box office dud,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.360 --> 00:03:48.000
but it also came into theaters with high&nbsp;
expectations and was absolutely terrible,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:51.200
wasting a star-studded cast and all its potential.

00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:55.680
Fiennes played secret agent John Steed&nbsp;
in this big budget adaptation of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.680 --> 00:04:00.240
hit British television series of the same&nbsp;
name. But despite having all the ingredients&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.240 --> 00:04:05.600
to be the next big action franchise, "The&nbsp;
Avengers" was a total disaster and a clumsy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.600 --> 00:04:11.120
charmless film that didn't exactly electrify&nbsp;
the box office like its MCU namesake.

00:04:11.680 --> 00:04:14.720
Fiennes himself slammed the&nbsp;
movie, telling The Guardian:

00:04:14.720 --> 00:04:17.360
"You don't go to work thinking&nbsp;
you're going to make a bad film.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.360 --> 00:04:20.800
I went to work thinking, 'Great,&nbsp;
let's reinvent 'The Avengers,''&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.800 --> 00:04:25.600
which I loved as a kid. It's only&nbsp;
now ... that we look back and groan."

00:04:25.600 --> 00:04:29.840
Actor Tom Felton came to fame thanks to his&nbsp;
casting in "Harry Potter," though he'd had a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.840 --> 00:04:34.800
few roles before joining the J.K. Rowling epic.&nbsp;
After leaving Hogwarts, Felton struggled to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:40.000
achieve the same success as the franchise's trio&nbsp;
of young stars. One film he took on in the wake&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:45.200
of "Harry Potter" that he almost certainly&nbsp;
regrets is the horror movie "Night Wolf."

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:49.440
A film that takes itself way more seriously&nbsp;
than it should, "Night Wolf" centers on a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.440 --> 00:04:54.880
group of teens in a cliched situation: stuck&nbsp;
inside a house during a dark and stormy night.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.880 --> 00:04:59.520
One by one, they get picked off by a&nbsp;
mysterious creature: a werewolf. Of course&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.520 --> 00:05:04.000
this comes as a complete shock to audiences&nbsp;
who didn't look at the title of the movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:09.280
or pick up the very obvious clues that the&nbsp;
filmmakers probably thought were ever-so-clever.

00:05:09.280 --> 00:05:13.440
Felton plays the stock stoner character&nbsp;
Gary, one of the beast's first victims,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.440 --> 00:05:16.880
so if you are checking this one&nbsp;
out because you love Draco Malfoy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.880 --> 00:05:20.880
don't expect to see much of him. He might be&nbsp;
glad he didn't have to stick around for the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:25.440
film's entire shoot, but he probably wishes he&nbsp;
hadn't been there at all. At least he was smart&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:25.440 --> 00:05:30.080
enough to not return for the director's&nbsp;
next movie, "Strippers vs. Werewolves."

00:05:30.080 --> 00:05:32.283
"I bet you loved that, didn't you, Potter?"

00:05:32.283 --> 00:05:37.520
Joining Hogwarts for "Harry Potter and the Goblet&nbsp;
of Fire," actor Brendan Gleeson played Mad Eye&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.520 --> 00:05:43.440
Moody, who is at first the disguise of Barty&nbsp;
Crouch Jr. In subsequent films, Gleeson returns as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:43.440 --> 00:05:49.440
the real Mad Eye, and helps Potter defeat the Dark&nbsp;
Lord Voldemort. A renowned Irish character actor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:49.440 --> 00:05:54.880
Gleeson's career goes all the way back to the late&nbsp;
'80s and he's gone on to feature in classics like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.880 --> 00:06:00.240
"Into The West," "Braveheart," and "28 Days&nbsp;
Later." His career also has its flops though,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.240 --> 00:06:04.240
and one actioner may be the film&nbsp;
the actor would love us all to skip.

00:06:04.240 --> 00:06:09.680
Though it boasted a decent cast, "Turbulence"&nbsp;
is decidedly not a '90s classic, no matter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:09.680 --> 00:06:15.040
what the filmmakers lofty ambitions may have&nbsp;
been. In the film, Gleeson stars as Stubbs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:15.040 --> 00:06:20.880
a bank robber being transported by plane alongside&nbsp;
another diabolical criminal named Weaver,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.880 --> 00:06:25.280
who manages to break free of his U.S.&nbsp;
Marshal escort and take over the flight.

00:06:25.280 --> 00:06:30.320
It may have been a compelling starting premise,&nbsp;
but with flat performances and unimpressive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:30.320 --> 00:06:35.760
stunts, "Turbulence" crashed and burned. The&nbsp;
film's stark similarities to "Con Air," released&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:35.760 --> 00:06:40.880
the same year, definitely didn't help matters&nbsp;
either. Gleeson spared himself the indignity&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.880 --> 00:06:45.840
of appearing in the two direct-to-video&nbsp;
sequels, which were somehow even worse.

00:06:52.514 --> 00:06:54.100
"...what?"

00:06:54.127 --> 00:06:59.440
A member of the Order of the Phoenix,&nbsp;
Remus Lupin started out as a mysterious&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:59.440 --> 00:07:04.560
figure in his first appearance, with many&nbsp;
believing that it was he, in werewolf form,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:04.560 --> 00:07:09.600
who had been terrorizing Hogwarts. But after&nbsp;
the culprit was revealed to be Peter Pettigrew,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:09.600 --> 00:07:13.440
Lupin became one of the greatest&nbsp;
heroes of the Second Wizarding War.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:13.440 --> 00:07:19.200
He was played by actor David Thewlis, who outside&nbsp;
of "Harry Potter" has had plenty of hit films.

00:07:19.200 --> 00:07:25.600
But the disaster "The Island of Dr. Moreau" was&nbsp;
most certainly not among them. A historically bad&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:25.600 --> 00:07:32.000
film, it was led by Marlon Brando as the eponymous&nbsp;
doctor, and boasted a star-studded cast. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:32.000 --> 00:07:37.280
it's Thewlis who sparks the film's story, as his&nbsp;
character crash lands on the island and discovers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:37.280 --> 00:07:43.120
the experiments of the demented Moreau, who is&nbsp;
creating bizarre, mutated half-human creatures.

00:07:43.120 --> 00:07:46.960
Thankfully, the film's failure&nbsp;
doesn't rest on Thewlis' shoulders.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:46.960 --> 00:07:50.800
That's down to Brando's laziness,&nbsp;
the film's haphazard construction,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:50.800 --> 00:07:55.840
and a muddled and meandering story. But&nbsp;
perhaps most importantly, it's just plain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:55.840 --> 00:08:00.960
boring. If Thewlis could back out of this&nbsp;
one retroactively, we have no doubt he would.

00:08:00.960 --> 00:08:08.298
"This is the most outrageous spectacle I&nbsp;
have ever witnessed. Look at yourself!"

00:08:08.298 --> 00:08:14.400
Actress Imelda Staunton went from little-known&nbsp;
character actor to most-hated woman in households&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:14.400 --> 00:08:18.080
everywhere when she gave her first&nbsp;
performance as the prudish professor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:18.080 --> 00:08:23.040
Dolores Umbridge. But just four years before she&nbsp;
came to fame in the Wizarding World, Staunton&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:23.040 --> 00:08:28.160
made a little film she now probably wishes she&nbsp;
could make disappear, "The Virgin of Liverpool."

00:08:28.160 --> 00:08:32.240
You'd be forgiven for thinking this one&nbsp;
was a groan-worthy adult comedy given&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:32.240 --> 00:08:37.280
its title and place on this list, but it's&nbsp;
actually about a statue of the Virgin Mary.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:37.280 --> 00:08:42.240
The film centers on a young girl who discovers&nbsp;
the statue when it is being discarded by a priest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:42.240 --> 00:08:47.040
during renovations of his church. While her family&nbsp;
is annoyed by the statue she brings home, it gets&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:47.040 --> 00:08:52.160
attention from the community for apparently&nbsp;
performing an active miracle in a chip shop.

00:08:52.160 --> 00:08:57.280
Aspiring to be a sappy sentimental family&nbsp;
movie, it ends up a groaner of a story that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:57.280 --> 00:09:02.400
looks incredibly cheap. So it comes as no surprise&nbsp;
to learn that the filmmakers made the movie just a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:02.400 --> 00:09:07.040
few weeks after finding a random script on the&nbsp;
internet. Thankfully, it wasn't bad enough to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:07.040 --> 00:09:12.849
prevent Staunton from being cast as one of Harry&nbsp;
Potter's most delightfully loathsome characters.

00:09:12.849 --> 00:09:20.720
"Deep down, you deserve to be&nbsp;
punished, don't you, Mr. Potter."

00:09:20.720 --> 00:09:25.920
Even more renowned than Dame Maggie Smith, Sir&nbsp;
Richard Harris led the first two "Harry Potter"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:25.920 --> 00:09:31.760
pictures as the wise, gentle wizard Dumbledore&nbsp;
before the star's unfortunate passing. But decades&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:31.760 --> 00:09:36.880
before he stepped onto Hogwarts' grounds, Harris&nbsp;
appeared in some of Hollywood's finest films, from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:36.880 --> 00:09:42.880
classics like "The Guns of Navarone" and "Mutiny&nbsp;
on the Bounty" to modern greats like "Unforgiven"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:42.880 --> 00:09:48.160
and "Patriot Games." But of course, like everyone&nbsp;
else on this list, he's got at least one that he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:48.160 --> 00:09:53.600
would take back if he could. In Harris' case,&nbsp;
it's the adventure movie, "Tarzan, The Ape Man."

00:09:57.840 --> 00:10:03.680
A modern reinterpretation of the classic novel by&nbsp;
Edgar Rice Burroughs, the film is not the rousing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:03.680 --> 00:10:09.120
tree-swinging adventure fans might have wanted&nbsp;
or even expected. That's because oddly enough,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:09.120 --> 00:10:14.000
Tarzan himself isn't even the star of the movie,&nbsp;
with the story instead focusing on his female&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:14.000 --> 00:10:19.520
companion Jane, and Harris playing her father&nbsp;
here. With Bo Derek cast in the role of Jane,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:19.520 --> 00:10:23.360
the producers turned the film into&nbsp;
little more than softcore titillation.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:23.360 --> 00:10:28.640
It's packed with enough uncomfortable adult&nbsp;
situations to make even John Waters blush.

00:10:28.640 --> 00:10:32.160
Derek was impressed with Harris'&nbsp;
professionalism and performance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:32.160 --> 00:10:35.600
despite the horrid script. She&nbsp;
even told Entertainment Weekly:

00:10:35.600 --> 00:10:39.436
"The picture was doomed. [...] But&nbsp;
Richard gave it his all anyway."

00:10:39.436 --> 00:10:44.880
Just 11 years old when he was cast as Ron Weasley&nbsp;
in "Harry Potter and the Sorcerer's Stone,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:44.880 --> 00:10:50.400
Rupert Grint hasn't achieved the same level of box&nbsp;
office stardom as his co-star Emma Watson. Nor has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:50.400 --> 00:10:54.960
he appeared in highly acclaimed arthouse films&nbsp;
like Daniel Radcliffe. He's preferred instead&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:54.960 --> 00:11:00.800
to stick to roles in prestige television projects,&nbsp;
such as "The ABC Murders" with John Malkovich and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:00.800 --> 00:11:05.520
"Snatch," a series adapted from the Guy Ritchie&nbsp;
film. But back when he was just getting started&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:05.520 --> 00:11:10.320
in "Harry Potter," Grint also starred in another&nbsp;
children's fantasy film: "Thunderpants," which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:10.320 --> 00:11:15.600
is about a boy who can't stop farting. Needless&nbsp;
to say, it didn't become a cinematic classic.

00:11:21.280 --> 00:11:25.760
While Grint does not take the title role in&nbsp;
"Thunderpants," he does play the best friend,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:25.760 --> 00:11:30.080
a child scientist who helps the tooter&nbsp;
deal with his worrisome wind-breaking.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:30.080 --> 00:11:34.800
In fairness to Grint, this ridiculous romp&nbsp;
isn't all that terrible. It's a fairly fun&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:34.800 --> 00:11:39.760
children's flick that will at least leave you&nbsp;
laughing from the ludicrous light-hearted gags.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:39.760 --> 00:11:42.960
But with Grint attempting a more&nbsp;
serious and dramatic career,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:42.960 --> 00:11:47.103
this can't be a movie he's proud to&nbsp;
trot out for his new fans to watch.

